The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
gtk_widget_get_preferred_size(widget, &min, &nat);
if (width < min.width || height < min.height)
```
Reason:
The use of `gtk_widget_get_preferred_size()` incorrectly determines the minimum dimensions for the popover by mixing up the minimum height for the minimum width and vice versa. This results in the popover being closed even when it could be displayed without generating a critical error.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
gtk_widget_measure(widget, GTK_ORIENTATION_VERTICAL, width, &min_height_for_width, NULL, NULL, NULL);
gtk_widget_measure(widget, GTK_ORIENTATION_HORIZONTAL, height, &min_width_for_height, NULL, NULL, NULL);
if (width < min_width_for_height || height < min_height_for_width)
```
Reason:
The patch replaces the incorrect `gtk_widget_get_preferred_size()` with `gtk_widget_measure()`, which correctly calculates the minimum height for the given width and the minimum width for the given height. This ensures that the popover is only closed when it truly cannot be displayed, thus fixing the bug.

